ce/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/2541e696df1d871e65d3717d03c2ce842f4312c6a86fd09ccc8f13e04d8d1216.png)\n\nNow, we determine the value of $Φ(0.75)$ from the table:\n\n- We first select the row that corresponds to $0.7$ and the column that corresponds to $0.05.$\n\n- Then, we take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7357\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, according to the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 0.75)=Φ(0.75)=0.7734.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77015ca5-d392-500e-93dc-8e065dd1c06c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f93a311d-c6e5-5785-b057-99cb01717c05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2538" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361063} {:answer/id #uuid "3baa6a94-2681-58ad-bbb9-f1fea9773cb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2061" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361064} {:answer/id #uuid "3c7e3b49-1a4d-51bb-8add-2d93712672b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2296" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361065} {:answer/id #uuid "8c59b7bf-e530-55dc-a64a-76cfb8e4bd8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1762" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361066} {:answer/id #uuid "64fb8d93-96ac-5830-b95f-21f75a5a7c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1736" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c59b7bf-e530-55dc-a64a-76cfb8e4bd8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1762" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361066} :answer-field/id #uuid "496ebf5d-279a-5bb5-98cc-f6fbb3df2101" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d21cc308-7cf1-53af-b965-44d97c4f0252" :question/math-academy-id "q-94104" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<-0.93).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1788\\,$ | $\\,0.1762\\,$ | $\\,0.1736\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ | $\\,0.2033\\,$ | $\\,0.2005\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.2358\\,$ | $\\,0.2327\\,$ | $\\,0.2296\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "If $Z∼N(0,1),$ then by the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nAlso, since $Z$ is continuous, \n\n$$\nP(Z<-0.93)=P(Z\\le -0.93)=Φ(-0.93).\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/0d1e28f38a69fb9b75d67ef1753f23ce01b6328a5bbcd30c7dfb7fd5e24caec4.png)\n\nNow, we determine the value of $Φ(-0.93)$ from the table:\n\n- We first select the row that corresponds to $-0.9$ and the column that corresponds to $0.03.$\n\n- Then, we take the value that lies at the intersection:\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1788\\,$ | $\\,0.1762\\,$ | $\\,0.1736\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ | $\\,0.2033\\,$ | $\\,0.2005\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.2358\\,$ | $\\,0.2327\\,$ | $\\,0.2296\\,$ |\n\nTherefore, according to the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le -0.93)=Φ(-0.93)=0.1762.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e376bffa-02ae-5575-af2c-4ad5e703f9fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "136e8c0b-3896-57d8-b40c-a703826bd3e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3124" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361070} {:answer/id #uuid "1427cf49-0a46-554a-b8be-5e91d1df9bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2867" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361071} {:answer/id #uuid "7e69030d-f8aa-5862-a59e-e4a8c2a0d198" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2967" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361072} {:answer/id #uuid "bb0addc0-4619-5414-bd6a-e420ef8fab7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3856" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361073} {:answer/id #uuid "3d43842e-4713-5583-9fbb-0e8f1cf8ba81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3557" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d43842e-4713-5583-9fbb-0e8f1cf8ba81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3557" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361074} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d894392-7feb-5488-bf61-3a12c0a75e79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82ed56ce-89c1-550b-9533-6d19a8ce65e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-94151" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z\\ge 0.37).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ | $\\,0.6406\\,$ | $\\,0.6443\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6736\\,$ | $\\,0.6772\\,$ | $\\,0.6808\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ | $\\,0.7123\\,$ | $\\,0.7157\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z\\ge 0.37).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/020f8a79730152c5c283dc8939e58f9ec44cf93b9f6727822df9de7447af8f5c.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSince the total area under the graph equals $1,$ we can express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge 0.37) & =1-P(Z<0.37) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.37)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/20c48d96e4941259d89303bdbfadd92125ad155bc068836ddeb510b655ec19a6.png)\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(0.37)=0.6443.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge 0.37) & =1-Φ(0.37) \\\\  & =1-0.6443 \\\\  & =0.3557.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e376bffa-02ae-5575-af2c-4ad5e703f9fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb37e1ad-99fc-51a6-b143-638a5ff3b919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0924" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361077} {:answer/id #uuid "4b378034-378b-5e53-8bce-8481b2f7d9cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0321" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361078} {:answer/id #uuid "7715dc0e-2434-50fd-94b3-a42e89df9d18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0865" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361079} {:answer/id #uuid "66add773-73dc-544b-abd5-6f283c1b5a81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1234" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361080} {:answer/id #uuid "da8ea0d9-9ed9-5d24-b957-3444137801cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0174" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #u