db/ref 17592186361082 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "607e0800-870c-5271-9220-0489d9c5b891" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b41b900-344d-5f56-b571-26542cb4a7bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2782" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361084} {:answer/id #uuid "40f1d376-49c7-52a1-be7a-997ac695c06b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2564" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361085} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b7ef66-e9be-504e-a1ce-789646bae3c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361086} {:answer/id #uuid "8feb120d-d218-5fbc-88c7-feaa019fc31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2632" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361087} {:answer/id #uuid "372e428a-79f0-5f66-b7bb-1deb023fbac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3245" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8feb120d-d218-5fbc-88c7-feaa019fc31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2632" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361087} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccaeca72-d670-572c-a30e-69fd78ad0132" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c275d1a6-1c72-56f0-ade4-3383858353be" :question/math-academy-id "q-94194" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-1.2<Z<-0.31).$\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1151\\,$ | $\\,0.1131\\,$ | $\\,0.1112\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1357\\,$ | $\\,0.1335\\,$ | $\\,0.1314\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.3085\\,$ | $\\,0.3050\\,$ | $\\,0.3015\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.3409\\,$ | $\\,0.3372\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3821\\,$ | $\\,0.3783\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1151\\,$ | $\\,0.1131\\,$ | $\\,0.1112\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1357\\,$ | $\\,0.1335\\,$ | $\\,0.1314\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.3085\\,$ | $\\,0.3050\\,$ | $\\,0.3015\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.3409\\,$ | $\\,0.3372\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3821\\,$ | $\\,0.3783\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-1.2<Z<-0.31).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/46b71217fcee1d130b3778ce2cd101aac9814870b71683656987d476e71412c1.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.2<Z<-0.31) & =P(Z<-0.31)-P(Z\\le -1.2) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.31)-P(Z\\le -1.2) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.31)-Φ(-1.2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.2) & =0.1151 \\\\ Φ(-0.31) & =0.3783\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.2<Z<-0.31) & =Φ(-0.31)-Φ(-1.2) \\\\  & =0.3783-0.1151 \\\\  & =0.2632.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "607e0800-870c-5271-9220-0489d9c5b891" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c678d4fd-83cd-5a52-902d-f8326f03b50c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0529" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059198} {:answer/id #uuid "25d9136a-3161-5664-ae6a-0c740c27d138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0987" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059199} {:answer/id #uuid "52cb0a29-8496-5646-b2a9-b0fae26959fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0678" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059200} {:answer/id #uuid "686a29b4-a276-5a84-9d45-572cada7cfcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0632" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059201} {:answer/id #uuid "6db45a8c-ae03-5810-8fad-d407afc80f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0543" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "686a29b4-a276-5a84-9d45-572cada7cfcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0632" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059201} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cdcc936-2d7f-5637-ba1c-776c3c6619db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd599733-7c2f-538f-a1fa-ca130a6c4dd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-94195" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(0.70<Z<0.92).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ |" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(0.70<Z<0.92).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/3eb46852c53e4fa13aaa29c31623153bfef604d138f15c6da67732d5730b785f.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.70<Z<0.92) & =P(Z<0.92)-P(Z\\le 0.70) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.92)-P(Z\\le 0.70) \\\\  & =Φ(0.92)-Φ(0.70)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.70) & =0.7580 \\\\ Φ(0.92) & =0.8212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.7<Z<0.92) & =Φ(0.92)-Φ(0.70) \\\\  & =0.8212-0.7580 \\\\  & =0.0632.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
